 "findings": [
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-fleet/pipelines/dispatch.yml",
   "fp": "90abb48824bb",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 54,
   "message": "The pipeline reads the trusted branch's `.specclaw/config.yaml` from `origin/$trusted` but never records which commit it read. That config decides vault, image, namespace, node_label, image_pull_secret and claude_version (directly, or through trusted_only_settings when the branch omits a key). The run record pins only `dispatched_commit` (the branch SHA), which does not reproduce inherited values. Fix: capture `git rev-parse origin/$trusted`, export it (for example FLEET_TRUSTED_COMMIT), and add it to record_run (`settings_commit=`). Apply the same change in dispatch-hosted.yml.",
   "original_severity": "major",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B5",
   "scenario": "The branch config has no `vault:` and inherits `vault: kv-a` from main at commit X. The run record shows dispatched_commit=<branch sha>, image=\u2026, and no vault or trusted revision. Main later changes to `vault: kv-b`, and the record can no longer tell which vault and credentials the run used.",
   "severity": "major"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-fleet/image/entrypoint.sh",
   "fp": "0184a924958d",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 71,
   "message": "A malformed FLEET_AGENT_TIMEOUT is silently replaced with 7200 instead of failing or recording a flag. Record a failure (for example exit=bad-agent-timeout), or at least log the fallback.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B6",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-fleet/lib/settings.sh",
   "fp": "655c9fee065f",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 3,
   "message": "FLEET_SECURE_KEYS leaves out `deadline_minutes` and `cluster_name`. A branch run can therefore set a Job deadline of up to 99999 minutes (activeDeadlineSeconds of about 69 days, spending the assignee's plan) and write any `cluster=` into the run record. Either add these keys to the trusted-only list or document why they are excluded.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B1",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-sync/bin/specclaw-azdo-issue",
   "fp": "6551cae0b58a",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 480,
   "message": "PY_RECORDS uses `.get(\"comments\", [])`. A 2xx JSON answer with no `comments` list is reported as 'no records' instead of failing, so `status` cannot tell 'could not read' from 'nothing there'. Require a list and exit non-zero otherwise.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B3",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
  {
   "file": "plugins/specclaw-fleet/lib/azdo-rest.sh",
   "fp": "5141607c9c15",
   "in_delta": true,
   "line": 5,
   "message": "The PAT-derived Basic auth header is passed on the curl command line, so other local users can see it in the process list. Pass it with `-H @-` or a `--config` file on stdin instead.",
   "original_severity": "minor",
   "pass": "review",
   "pre_existing": false,
   "rule": "B8",
   "scenario": "",
   "severity": "minor"
  },
